7. INTENT PROCESSING

The Intelligence Server receives or coordinates the interpretation of human intent.

Example:

User:

"Create a task for the API documentation."

The Server must determine:

- What the user intends.
- Which context is relevant.
- Which capability is required.
- Which permissions apply.
- Whether execution is local or external.
- Which integration or service can provide the capability.
- Whether confirmation is necessary.


8. CONTEXT

The Intelligence Server consumes relevant contextual information from the iRiel Context architecture.

Context may include:

- Current activity.
- Active project.
- Recent interactions.
- Relevant task state.
- Current environment.
- Previous decisions.
- Relevant memory.
- User-defined preferences.
- Workflow state.

The Intelligence Server should not require unrestricted access to all user context.

Only context relevant to the operation should be used.


9. MEMORY

The Intelligence Server may interact with memory systems when memory is relevant to the requested operation.

Memory is not automatically created from every interaction.

Canonical flow:

Interaction
    ↓
Context Evaluation
    ↓
Memory Decision
    ↓
Persist / Do Not Persist


10. GOVERNANCE

Governance is evaluated before controlled execution.

Canonical flow:

Intent
    ↓
Capability
    ↓
Governance
    ↓
Authorization
    ↓
Execution

Governance may:

- Allow execution.
- Deny execution.
- Require confirmation.
- Restrict data.
- Restrict capabilities.
- Restrict integrations.
- Require additional authorization.


11. INTELLIGENCE ROUTER

The Intelligence Router operates within the broader Intelligence architecture.

It determines the appropriate intelligence resource, capability or execution path.

It may evaluate:

- Capability match.
- Context match.
- Privacy.
- Latency.
- Cost.
- Availability.
- Reliability.
- Provider capability.
- User authorization.


12. AI-AGNOSTIC ARCHITECTURE

The Intelligence Server must remain independent from any single AI provider.

Possible intelligence resources include:

- Local models.
- OpenAI models.
- Gemini models.
- Claude models.
- Other compatible models.
- Specialized local intelligence.
- Future intelligence systems.

The ecosystem may change providers without changing the identity or fundamental architecture of @iriel.


