19. LOCAL-FIRST PROCESSING

The Intelligence Server should prefer local execution when the requested capability can be fulfilled locally and doing so satisfies the applicable requirements.

Canonical preference:

Local
    ↓
Authorized Personal Infrastructure
    ↓
External Service


20. EXTERNAL PROCESSING

External execution may occur when:

- The capability is unavailable locally.
- The user authorizes external processing.
- The requested service requires external infrastructure.
- Governance permits external processing.
- External execution provides a necessary capability.


21. PRIVACY BY DEFAULT

The Intelligence Server must treat personal data as private by default.

External transmission must be:

- Necessary.
- Authorized.
- Policy-compliant.
- Minimized.
- Protected.


22. DATA MINIMIZATION

The Intelligence Server should provide integrations and external services with only the information necessary to execute the requested capability.

Example:

task.create

Required:

- Task title.
- Task description.
- Destination.

Not automatically required:

- Entire user memory.
- Entire context history.
- Unrelated files.
- Private communications.
- Unrelated personal data.


23. CREDENTIAL ISOLATION

AI models should not directly receive sensitive integration credentials.

